LQS = [
    (('Write in detail the chemical composition and some of the prominent chemical and physical properties of the following material: a. Plastic b. Polythene c. Glass', 'درج ذیل اشیا کی کیمیائی ترکیب اور نمایاں کیمیائی و طبعی خصوصیات تفصیل سے لکھیں: الف۔ پلاسٹک ب۔ پولیتھین ج۔ شیشہ', 'د لاندې توکو کیمیاوي ترکیب او مهم کیمیاوي او فزیکي خواص په تفصیل ولیکئ: الف. پلاستیک ب. پولیتین ج. ښیښه'),
     'Plastic: a synthetic high-molecular-weight chain molecule (polymer), mostly carbon/organic, sometimes mixed with other ingredients; versatile, light, flexible, moisture resistant, durable, strong, cheap, clear or opaque; chains flow past each other on moderate heating and it decomposes around 200°C (392°F). Polythene: formed from polymers of ethene; tough, white, translucent, waxy thermoplastic that softens on heating; low-density form by high-pressure polymerization of ethene, high-density form at lower pressure with catalysts; does not readily biodegrade. Glass: amorphous (non-crystalline) solid; man-made glass is silica (SiO2) + soda + lime + colouring additives, heated to about 982°C; brittle, transparent, strong, minimally conducting and unreactive with stored materials; soda lowers silica\'s fusion point; it behaves as a rigid liquid and can be remelted and recycled.'),
    (('Compare hydrogen with helium. Which element is better to be used in balloons?', 'ہائیڈروجن اور ہیلیم کا موازنہ کریں۔ غباروں کے لیے کون سا عنصر بہتر ہے؟', 'هایډروجن او هیلیم پرتله کړئ. په بالونونو کې کوم عنصر غوره دی؟'),
     'Hydrogen: most abundant element, colourless, diatomic, lightest gas, highly flammable and forms explosive mixtures with air. Helium: noble (inert) gas, second most abundant, forms no compounds, atom of 2 protons, 2 neutrons and 2 electrons. Both are lighter than air so balloons rise, and hydrogen is even lighter, but a slight spark can make a hydrogen balloon explode. Helium is therefore better and safer for balloons.'),
    (('Write the chemical and physical properties of copper and compare it with aluminum. Justify which element is better suited to be used in wiring.', 'تانبے کی کیمیائی اور طبعی خصوصیات لکھ کر ایلومینیم سے موازنہ کریں۔ وائرنگ کے لیے کون سا بہتر ہے؟', 'د مس کیمیاوي او فزیکي خواص ولیکئ او له المونیم سره یې پرتله کړئ. سیم کشۍ ته کوم غوره دی؟'),
     'Copper: malleable (sheets 1/500 inch), ductile, second only to silver in electrical conductivity, excellent heat conductor, corrosion resistant, moderately active, dissolves in alkalis and forms hydrated copper carbonate Cu2(OH)2CO3 in moist air. Aluminum: shiny, silvery, light and strong, protected by an oxide layer, burns in oxygen to Al2O3. For wiring copper is better: 1.6 times the current-carrying capacity, easier to install, resists corrosion, and its full life-cycle cost is lower, whereas aluminum cable is harder to install and more prone to failure.'),
    (('Give a brief description about different materials which can be used in thermometers. Based on their nature justify which is the most suited material for thermometer.', 'تھرمامیٹر میں استعمال ہونے والے مختلف مادوں کی مختصر وضاحت کریں اور بتائیں کہ کون سا سب سے موزوں ہے۔', 'په تودوخې میچ کې د کارېدونکو بېلابېلو توکو لنډ بیان وکړئ او ثابت کړئ چې کوم تر ټولو مناسب دی.'),
     'Water freezes at 0°C and its boiling/freezing points vary with pressure, so it is unsuitable (it is used only as a calibration standard). Alcohol has a low freezing point and expands well in capillary tubes, so it suits low temperatures, but its low boiling point makes high temperatures hard to measure. Mercury has a low freezing point and a high boiling point, so it is ideal for measuring most temperatures, though it is expensive and dangerous. Mercury is therefore the most suited (alcohol for very low temperatures).'),
    (('Write three examples of chemical changes which we encounter in our daily life.', 'روزمرہ زندگی میں کیمیائی تبدیلیوں کی تین مثالیں لکھیں۔', 'په ورځني ژوند کې د کیمیاوي بدلون درې بېلګې ولیکئ.'),
     '1. Burning: wood and other organic matter combine with O2, giving carbon dioxide, water and heat. 2. Rusting: iron combines with atmospheric oxygen to form iron oxide. 3. Fermentation: yeast or bacteria convert sugar into acid or alcohol in oxygen-free conditions (dough, curds). (Others: respiration, decomposition.)'),
    (('Describe the harmful impacts of CFCs, pesticides and fertilizers.', 'سی ایف سی، کیڑے مار ادویات اور کھادوں کے نقصان دہ اثرات بیان کریں۔', 'د CFCs، د آفتونو ضد درملو او سرو زیانمن اغېز بیان کړئ.'),
     'CFCs released from refrigerators, freezers and air conditioners react with ozone in the upper atmosphere and weaken its protection against UV radiation; more UV causes skin cancer and weakens the immune system and skin defenses. Pesticides: organophosphates and carbamates affect the nervous system; others irritate skin and eyes, may be carcinogens or affect the hormone (endocrine) system. Fertilizers: toxic chemicals enter the food chain and seep into groundwater; nitrates and nitrites cause blue-baby syndrome, and heavy metals (mercury, lead, cadmium, uranium) can damage kidneys, lungs and liver.'),
    (('Recycling is the need of the day. Different types of waste material like plastic, glass, rubber etc if not recycled can pose serious threats to environment. Elaborate the statement.', 'ری سائیکلنگ وقت کی ضرورت ہے۔ پلاسٹک، شیشہ، ربڑ وغیرہ اگر ری سائیکل نہ ہوں تو ماحول کے لیے سنگین خطرہ ہیں۔ اس بیان کی وضاحت کریں۔', 'ریسایکلینګ د وخت اړتیا ده. پلاستیک، ښیښه، رابړ او نور که ریسایکل نه شي چاپېریال ته جدي ګواښ دي. دا خبره تشریح کړئ.'),
     'Earth\'s resources are being used up too fast; recycling with reduced consumption is our best defence. Unrecycled plastic and polythene do not readily biodegrade and stay in landfills for hundreds of years, harming health and environment; rubber waste (tyres) is hard to dispose of. Recycling saves raw materials and energy and cuts CO2: glass is 100% recyclable without loss of quality; recycled copper uses only 15% of the energy of mining; aluminum cans return to shelves in about 60 days; recovered rubber costs about half and saves petroleum; recycled iron is cheaper and less damaging than extraction from ores; plastic can be remade into pellets and new bottles.'),
]

